# Project safety

## Release and privacy

- No push, tag, GitHub Release, or package publish without explicit owner request
- No private user data, personal wordlists, maintainer paths, or credentials in public commits
- Effective project context comes from the wordlist path — do not assume cwd alone

## Mutation safety

- Project operation lock required for all mutating operations
- Preview and execution share one immutable prepared object (`PreparedPush`, `PreparedTargetSettingsUpdate`, etc.)
- Confirmation binds to exact plan/update ID; fingerprint re-checked before write
- Stale preview must not execute; no automatic re-plan after confirmation
- Pending Recovery blocks new write operations
- No automatic Pull, Push, or Recovery

## Engineering discipline

- Minimal diff — no drive-by refactors or parallel reimplementations of existing paths
- Run focused tests for changed scope, then full `scripts/ci.sh`
- Do not stop on red tests; do not mask failures with meaningless coverage tests

## Workspace snapshot

Before the final user report on modifying tasks: remove stale archives, create `$HOME/code.zip`
with `--force`, verify with `--check`, end report with `CODE_ARCHIVE` and `SHA256`. Skill:
`create-code-snapshot` in spell-sync-dev. Read-only tasks skip recreation.

Recovery protocol details: `@docs/RECOVERY.md`
